Which step of a static validation stopped, and whether it stopped or threw.

SecStaticCodeCheckValidity was already known to be where MoneyMoney sat; these are the steps it is
made of, one line each. The application runs this on a background thread while its main thread keeps
animating a spinner, so a validation that never finishes looks exactly like an application that is
merely slow: window up, run loop turning, nothing wrong on any log.

AND THE CATCH BLOCKS PRINT TOO, WHICH IS THE PART I GOT WRONG FIRST. A call line with no back line
means hung OR THREW, and I read it as hung for a whole rung. validateNonResourceComponents never
printed a return and had not blocked at all: it threw, and the application went on to show its own
damaged-bundle alert. With the catch instrumented the answer is one line,

    CIDER_CSSTEP core threw MacOSError error=-67061

which is errSecCSSignatureFailed. So the code signature verification REJECTS this bundle, where
macOS accepts it, and that is the next thing to explain.

